                            <comment id="16407624" author="alex_pl" created="Wed, 21 Mar 2018 08:57:26 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=dpavlov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;dpavlov&quot;&gt;dpavlov&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-5958&quot; title=&quot;Ignite Cache 3: IgniteTopologyValidatorGridSplitCacheTest.testTopologyValidator  fails&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-5958&quot;&gt;IGNITE-5958&lt;/a&gt; is not actual anymore. There was a race in the old implementation which was fixed by &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-6491&quot; title=&quot;Race in TopologyValidator.validate() and EVT_NODE_LEFT listener calls (split-brain activator)&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-6491&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-6491&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-6519&quot; title=&quot;Race in SplitAwareTopologyValidator on activator and server node join&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-6519&quot;&gt;IGNITE-6519&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-5870&quot; title=&quot;IgniteTopologyValidatorGridSplitCacheTest#testTopologyValidator fails&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-5870&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-5870&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; don&apos;t contain any stack traces, but I think it&apos;s the same problem as &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-5958&quot; title=&quot;Ignite Cache 3: IgniteTopologyValidatorGridSplitCacheTest.testTopologyValidator  fails&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-5958&quot;&gt;IGNITE-5958&lt;/a&gt; and ticket can be closed as duplicate.&lt;br/&gt;
Fix for this ticket also affect testTopologyValidator, so after merge testTopologyValidator can be unmuted.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
